cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these cases, scorers or runner, please cite the exact version you used, as below."
type: software
title: "Invalid State Admissions Benchmark: admission cases and disposition scorer"
version: "2.0.0"
abstract: "A benchmark for what stateful AI systems write into shared state. Version 2.0.0: 39 synthetic cases in 12 families, with system-visible inputs separated from ground truth; declared rules and target contracts; a Level 1 disposition scorer and a Level 2 stateful runner that scores persisted records and served answers through an architecture-neutral adapter contract; metrics OAR, IPAR, VSAR, CDR, SRA, UFR, DLR and CPR, with critical failures and exact intervals. Baselines: three trivial and one non-LLM reference baseline (measured), and a harness for three proposed language-model baselines (not run). No result is reported for any AI system. v1.0.0 files are kept unchanged under v1/."
authors:
  - name: "Tinor"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23447898
url: "https://tinor.io/journal/toward-zero-invalid-state-admissions"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tinor-Tech/invalid-state-admissions-benchmark"
